-- ownership: a member met three times or more in one positions tree
-- (ownership-v2.md §2.3 *Saturation at two*). The constructor rebuilds the
-- tree with each member at most twice, which changes no verdict, and no
-- snapshot of the new value keys a node the rebuild dropped: the
-- ReleaseSafe compiler checks it. `[ x, y, x, x ]` drops `[ x, x ]`'s
-- node, and so does the spread over `[ x, y ]`.
pub literal : List Int, List Int → List (List Int)
literal x y = [ x, y, x, x ]


pub spread : List Int, List Int → List (List Int)
spread x y =
    a = [ x, y ]
    [ …a, x, x ]
